	(text "Notes\n1. Power the heart beat module from 3V3, never 5V: no analog pin may see more than 3.3 V.\n2. Cover the module's own LED with black tape (or remove it), or its light swamps the reading.\n3. Test setup: D1 faces the module's detector 1-2 cm away inside a short black tube (light-tight).\n    The app flashes D1 at known rates (1-60 Hz, short pulses, steps) and reads A2 and A3 at 1000/s.\n4. R1/C1 is a 1st-order low-pass (~72 Hz): cuts screen PWM flicker (480 Hz -> ~15%) and\n    stretches very short strobe flashes so they are not missed between readings.\n5. D1: white LED, to match real-world light. LED current ~ (5 - 3.0 V) / 100 R ~ 20 mA.\n    Q1: any small NPN (2N3904, BC547, 2N2222); check the pinout, BC547 is C-B-E.\n6. Q2/R4 (not fitted): fallback detector on A1 if the module is IR-only or too slow.\n7. On the wearable, a short black tube in front of the detector narrows its view to where the wearer looks."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "019157da-934f-5f15-9e86-1ca9e4a5d1fc")
	)
	(text "Detector + anti-alias filter"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 88.9 64.77 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(bold yes)
			)
